// Sample-and-Hold Melody — Rhythmic and Sequenced — from Synth Templates card sample-and-hold-melody (schema synth-template-card/0.2)
// Generated by card-to-pdl.py: card words → vocabulary.yaml numbers → VCV Fundamental knobs. Do not edit; edit the card.
# voices: 1

@OSC1 = VCO
@FILT1 = VCF
@AMP = VCA
@AENV = ADSR
@LFO2 = LFO

// ── Signal flow ──
OSC1:SQR -> FILT1:IN
FILT1:LPF -> AMP:IN
AMP:OUT -> OUT:IN1    // fx skipped
AMP:OUT -> OUT:IN2

// ── Modulation ──
LFO2:SQR -> AMP:CV
KEYBOARD:PITCH -> OSC1:V/OCT
KEYBOARD:GATE -> AENV:GATE

// ── Parameters ──
* OSC1: FREQ = 0 | PW = 0.3
* FILT1: FREQ = 0.72 | RES = 0.25
* AMP: LEVEL = 0.8 | RESPONSE = 1.0
* AENV: A = 0.178 | D = 0.571 | S = 0.7 | R = 0.379
* LFO2: FREQ = 2.17 | OFFSET = 0.0

// ── Not carried into PDL ──
// block fx: fx chain (delay)
// block lfo1: s&h LFO (LFO has sine, triangle, saw, square outputs)
// audio ['amp', 'fx']: edge through fx (no fx module; the voice goes straight out)
// route lfo1 → osc1.pitch: route from an unmapped block (lfo1)
// route aenv → amp.level: input conflict (one cable per jack) (input AMP:CV already taken by lfo2)
// approximated: lfo2: tempo sync asked; LFO is free-running
